{"availability":"available","full":"LegoX/Lego-RL","name":"Lego-RL","description":"Lego-RL: Harness-Native Reinforcement Learning for Coding Agents","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":119,"forks":10,"created":"2026-07-28T06:28:16Z","updated":"2026-10-11T00:53:38Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lego-rl.pages.dev/docs","topics":[],"demo":"https://lego-rl.pages.dev/docs/demo","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:39.078Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:39.078Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:39.078Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:08.485Z","stars":111,"forks":9},{"at":"2026-10-12T09:45:27.527Z","stars":115,"forks":9},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:17:39.078Z","stars":119,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Online reinforcement learning for coding agents in their native harnesses and real repositories.","Lego-RL is an open-source framework for training coding agents with online reinforcement learning on real software-engineering tasks. It connects Claude Code, OpenHands, and OpenCode to verl while keeping each agent's native control flow.","Each run follows the same loop: an agent works on a repository task in a fresh Harbor sandbox, the task's verifier supplies the reward, and verl updates the policy from the captured trajectory."],"features":["Native agents: Claude Code, OpenHands, and OpenCode run through thin adapters. A custom","scaffold that speaks the OpenAI or Anthropic API can use the same agent-loop interface.","Faithful rollouts: an in-process proxy","records token ids, masks, and log-probabilities at generation time. It also handles history rewrites and serves the OpenAI and Anthropic interfaces used by the supported agents.","RL and scaling: PPO, GRPO, GSPO, and SAO"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LegoX/Lego-RL/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1d2cc40ca513ae71b5ece2c8d3ac78b91be1bf856118f9a1588883f7ee1a631c","extractedA